    "bottomLine": "The pick for faded, set-in stains on driveways and garage floors when you can give it time.",
    "description": "Terminator-HSD is a microbial oil stain remover sold as a powder that you mix with water and brush into the stain. Instead of emulsifying oil for a rinse, it introduces hydrocarbon-digesting microbes that break oil down where it sits, which is why it can reach stains that degreasers only lighten. The manufacturer positions it for old, set-in oil on concrete, asphalt and pavers. The routine is simple but patient: clean the surface, apply the mixture, keep it damp, and avoid rinsing for the time the label specifies. Owners commonly report that stains look unchanged for the first few days and then fade over the following week or two. It works best above roughly 50 degrees Fahrenheit and stalls in cold garages. Because it avoids solvents, it is one of the few strong options that is safe on blacktop. Do not use bleach or disinfecting cleaners on the area before or during treatment, as they kill the microbes. Expect roughly $20 to $35 for a container at the time of writing."
