        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy by stain age. Keep Oil-Dri granules and a degreaser concentrate like Oil Eater on hand for fresh spills, reach for Pour-N-Restore or a homemade diatomaceous earth poultice when a stain has had weeks to set, and use Terminator-HSD for old, faded garage floor halos you can leave alone for a week or two.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you use, absorb first, keep cleaners wet while they work, judge on dry concrete, and rinse responsibly. Then seal the slab and fix the leak, so you only have to do this once.
          </p>
